    All Sylow p-subgroups of $G$ are conjugate to each other for a fixed $p$.\\
    \textbf{iii. The Third Sylow Theorem:}\\
    $n_p \equiv 1 (\text{mod}\ p)$, where $n_p$ is the number of Sylow p-subgroups of G.
