    \textbf{• Sylow p-group} is defined as a group of order $p^am$, where $p \nmid m$, a subgroup of order $p^a$ is called a Sylow p-subgroup of $G$. $Syl_p(G)$ is the set of Sylow p-subgroups of $G$.
    \end{minipage}
};
