	\item Consider Newton's method with step size $1$, i.e. 
	\[N(x) = x - \frac{f'(x)}{f''(x)}. \]
	For which initializations $x_0$ does this method converge, oscillate and diverge? (Hint: You can run a numerical experiment to get a clue.)
\end{enumerate}

\end{document}

